Patch summary:
Route vkCmdPipelineBarrier2KHR through the global state.

Both decoders forwarded vkCmdPipelineBarrier2KHR straight to the driver, while
vkCmdPipelineBarrier and vkCmdPipelineBarrier2 go through the global state,
which decompresses emulated ETC2/ASTC images when they become readable and
tracks image layouts. Guests such as ANGLE record image barriers with the KHR
alias, so those transitions skipped decompression. VkDependencyInfoKHR is an
alias of VkDependencyInfo, so reuse on_vkCmdPipelineBarrier2.

diff --git a/host/vulkan/vk_decoder.cpp b/host/vulkan/vk_decoder.cpp
index 373a4a2..dbb548e 100644
--- a/host/vulkan/vk_decoder.cpp
+++ b/host/vulkan/vk_decoder.cpp
@@ -17288,7 +17288,11 @@ size_t VkDecoder::Impl::decode(void* buf, size_t len, IOStream* ioStream,
                                    (unsigned long long)pDependencyInfo);
                 }
                 if (CC_LIKELY(vk)) {
-                    vk->vkCmdPipelineBarrier2KHR(unboxed_commandBuffer, pDependencyInfo);
+                    // Route through the global state like vkCmdPipelineBarrier2 so emulated
+                    // compressed images (ETC2/ASTC) are decompressed and image layouts tracked.
+                    (void)unboxed_commandBuffer;
+                    m_state->on_vkCmdPipelineBarrier2(&m_pool, snapshotApiCallHandle, commandBuffer,
+                                                      pDependencyInfo);
                 }
                 vkStream->unsetHandleMapping();
                 if (m_snapshotsEnabled) {
